<file path="patches/0001-S1TMS-7-drop-and-count-queue-overflow-and-NULL-safe-.patch">
From ac807ca3fdd07675c23462afdf3fe71fac683297 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neal <nealpunjabi196@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:53:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] S1TMS-7: drop-and-count queue overflow and NULL-safe
 queue operations

- VehicleQueue gains a dropped counter; enqueue on a full queue leaves the
  queue unchanged and counts the vehicle as dropped
- queue functions accept NULL without crashing; dequeue leaves *vehicle
  untouched when the queue is empty
- add tests/test_queue_integrity.c (FIFO, wrap-around, exact-capacity and
  capacity+1 boundaries, empty dequeue, conservation) and tests/test_util.h

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015D1Ltje8dSmxKDaSCetk2G
---
 queue.c                      |  18 +++-
 queue.h                      |  12 +++
 tests/test_queue_integrity.c | 173 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/test_util.h            |  37 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 237 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/test_queue_integrity.c
 create mode 100644 tests/test_util.h

