<file path="patches/0002-CI-build-every-module-and-test-automatically-add-OS-.patch">
From 382c5723443cabb43c4422f62324d0a3ee54d121 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neal <nealpunjabi196@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 08:55:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] CI: build every module and test automatically; add OS
 matrix and memory checks

- compile all *.c modules (except the two programs with their own main) so new
  modules and every tests/test_*.c are picked up without editing the workflow
- build and smoke-test traffic_simulation.c, which CI previously never compiled
- run on ubuntu, macOS and Windows (NFR-005), fail-fast off so one OS cannot
  hide another's result
- add AddressSanitizer + UBSan job and a Valgrind job (S1TMS-7 memory criterion)
- drop the busy-wait-era `timeout` wrapper (not available on macOS runners)

