From: Neal <nealpunjabi196@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:00:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] S1TMS-9: tick-based simulation engine with per-direction
 queues and summary report

- simulation module: one bounded queue per direction, round-robin
  green/yellow/red signals, arrivals then departures each tick, per-tick
  callback for display; configuration validated before every run
- stats module: vehicles generated/processed/dropped/queued, average wait,
  maximum queue length, and a conservation check
  (generated = processed + dropped + queued); report printed at end of run
- main.c now drives the engine instead of the busy-wait loop (which spun a CPU
  core for the whole signal duration) and prints queue length and signal state
  per direction every tick, then the summary. Same two prompts as before
- tests/test_stats.c and tests/test_simulation.c: boundary values, hand-computed
  scenarios (waits, peak queue, overflow drops, multi-release), only-green-moves,
  conservation across a parameter sweep, repeatability

